formation\nTreasurer FAQ\nTitles and Registration\nApplication Forms\nUnclaimed Property State Treasurer\nBoating Registrations\nProperty Tax Payment Information\nHours\nMon\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nTue\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nWed\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nThu\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nFri\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nSat\nClosed\nSun\nClosed\nHome\nDepartments\nTreasurer\nTreasurer Office\nShelly Denniston |\nDeputy |\nDuties of the County Treasurer\nThe County Treasurer’s Office is responsible for a wide range of essential financial and administrative services for the residents of Otoe County. Key responsibilities include:\nRevenue Collection : Collecting all county revenues, including property taxes and fees.\nTax Billing and Collection : Billing and collecting real estate and personal property taxes.\nMotor Vehicle Services : Registering all motor vehicles with a tax situs in the county.\nDriver Licensing : Issuing driver licenses, commercial driver licenses (CDLs), learner’s permits, school permits, and state identification cards.\nDistribution of Funds : Disbursing collected funds to appropriate political subdivisions and taxing entities.\nBoat and Snowmobile Registration : Processing registrations for boats and snowmobiles.\nFor more information or to access services, please contact the County Treasurer’s Office or visit our office in person.\nInformational Materials Available\nC.D.L books\nDriver license books\nProvisional operator permits\nSpecialty license plate applications\nDocument Center\nThe Document Center provides easy access to public documents. Click on one of the categories below to see related documents or use the search function.\nSearch for file name:\nCategories always sorted by seq (sub-categories sorted within each category)\nDocuments sorted by SEQ in Ascending Order within category\nRESET\nTax Sale 3 documents\nBuyer pre-registration form\ndocument seq\n0.00\nW-9 Form\ndocument seq\n0.00\nTax Sale Instructions\ndocument seq\n0.00\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nTranslate\nEngli